      "short_title": "MetaAct",
      "source_hits": [
        "s2-citations"
      ],
      "summary_en": "MetaAct synthesizes executable action constraints from successful and failed trajectories, checks false blocks through log replay, and uses counterexamples for revision. Accepted constraints persist in deployment. Compilation and blocking mechanisms remain fixed, and the retirement monitor was inactive in the reported results.",
      "summary_zh": "MetaAct 从成功与失败轨迹合成可执行动作约束，利用日志回放检查误拦截并将反例用于修订；被接受的约束可持续部署。实验中的编译与拦截机制固定，退役监视器未实际触发。",
      "title": "MetaAct: Self-Evolving Executable Action Constraints for Embodied Language Agents",
      "updated": "2026-11-16T07:11:07Z",
      "version": 1,
